      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Given the problem:\n- \\( A + B + C + D = 36 \\)\n- \\( A + 2 = B - 2 = C \\times 2 = D \\div 2 \\)\n\nWe will define \\( x \\) as the common value of all expressions:\n\\[ A + 2 = x \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad A = x - 2 \\]\n\\[ B - 2 = x \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad B = x + 2 \\]\n\\[ C \\times 2 = x \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad C = \\frac{x}{2} \\]\n\\[ D \\div 2 = x \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad D = 2x \\]\n\nNext, we sum these variables:\n\\[ (x - 2) + (x + 2) + \\left( \\frac{x}{2} \\right) + 2x \\]\n\nCombine the terms:\n\\[ (x - 2 + x + 2 + \\frac{x}{2} + 2x) = 4x + \\frac{x}{2} \\]\n\\[ = \\frac{8x}{2} + \\frac{x}{2} = \\frac{9x}{2} \\]\n\nGiven that the sum equals 36:\n\\[ \\frac{9x}{2} = 36 \\]\n\nSolve for \\( x \\):\n\\[ 9x = 72 \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{72}{9} \\]\n\\[ x = 8 \\]\n\nFinally, find the individual values of \\( A \\), \\( B \\), \\( C \\), and \\( D \\):\n\\[ A = x - 2 = 8 - 2 = 6 \\]\n\\[ B = x + 2 = 8 + 2 = 10 \\]\n\\[ C = \\frac{x}{2} = \\frac{8}{2} = 4 \\]\n\\[ D = 2x = 2 \\times 8 = 16 \\]\n\nCompute the product \\( A \\times B \\times C \\times D \\):\n\\[ A \\times B \\times C \\times D = 6 \\times 10 \\times 4 \\times 16 \\]\n\nFirst \\( 6 \\times 10 = 60 \\):\n\\[ 60 \\times 4 = 240 \\]\n\\[ 240 \\times 16 \\]\n\nBreak down \\( 240 \\times 16 \\):\n\\[ 240 \\times 16 = 240 \\times (10 + 6) = (240 \\times 10) + (240 \\times 6) \\]\n\\[ 240 \\times 10 = 2400 \\]\n\\[ 240 \\times 6 = 1440 \\]\n\\[ 2400 + 1440 = 3840 \\]\n\nThus, the product \\( A \\times B \\times C \\times D \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{3840}\n\\]",
