      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Given the equation \\( 2(A + 2) = B - 2 \\), we first simplify it to:\n\\[ 2(A + 2) = B - 2 \\]\n\\[ 2A + 4 = B - 2 \\]\n\\[ B = 2A + 6 \\]\n\nSimilarly, from the equation \\( C \\times 2 = 2(A + 2) \\), we simplify to:\n\\[ C \\times 2 = 2(A + 2) \\]\n\\[ C = A + 2 \\]\n\nThe final equation involving \\( D \\) is \\( D \\div 2 = 2(A + 2) \\), which simplifies to:\n\\[ D \\div 2 = 2(A + 2) \\]\n\\[ D = 4(A + 2) \\]\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for \\( B \\), \\( C \\), and \\( D \\) into the sum equation:\n\\[ A + B + C + D = 36 \\]\n\\[ A + (2A + 6) + (A + 2) + 4(A + 2) = 36 \\]\n\\[ A + 2A + 6 + A + 2 + 4A + 8 = 36 \\]\n\\[ 8A + 16 = 36 \\]\n\\[ 8A = 20 \\]\n\\[ A = \\frac{20}{8} \\]\n\\[ A = \\frac{5}{2} \\]\n\nTherefore:\n\\[ B = 2 \\left( \\frac{5}{2} \\right) + 6 = 5 + 6 = 11 \\]\n\\[ C = \\frac{5}{2} + 2 = \\frac{5}{2} + \\frac{4}{2} = \\frac{9}{2} \\]\n\\[ D = 4 \\left( \\frac{5}{2} + 2 \\right) = 4 \\times \\frac{9}{2} = 18 \\]\n\nThe problem asks for the product \\( A \\times B \\times C \\times D \\):\n\\[ A \\times B \\times C \\times D = \\frac{5}{2} \\times 11 \\times \\frac{9}{2} \\times 18 \\]\n\nLet's calculate the product step by step:\n\n\\[ \\left( \\frac{5}{2} \\times 11 \\right) = \\frac{55}{2} \\]\n\\[ \\left( \\frac{55}{2} \\times \\frac{9}{2} \\right) = \\frac{495}{4} \\]\n\\[ \\left( \\frac{495}{4} \\times 18 \\right) = \\frac{495 \\times 18}{4} = \\frac{8910}{4} = 2227.5 \\]\n\nSo, the value is \\(\\boxed{2227.5}\\).",
